hadiths[35]{hadithnumber,text}:
"25401","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Said ibn al-Jubayr that a man who has approval (as a relater of hadith)"
"25402","Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Said ibn al-Jubayr that a man who has approval (as a relater of hadith)"
"25501","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Dhakwan Abu Amr - and he was a slave of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and she had freed him after her death - used to stand and recite for her in Ramadan."
"25502","Yahya related to me from Malik, from Abu an-Nadr, the freed slave of Umar ibn Ubaydillah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd ar-Rahman, from Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, that she said: \I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah"," may Allah bless him and grant him peace"," with my feet in his qiblah. When he prostrated"," he would nudge me"," and I would pull my feet up. When he stood"," I would stretch them out.\"" She said: \""And the houses at that time did not have lamps.\"""""
"256","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father from A'isha"
"257","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ismail from Ibn Abi Hakim that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah"
"258","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from his father that Umar ibn al-Khattab used to pray as much as Allah willed in the night until at the end of the night he would wake his family for the prayer. He used to say to them"
"259","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"260","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"261","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr from A'isha"
"262","Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf that he asked A'isha"
"263","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha"
"264","Yahya related to me from Malik from Makhrama ibn Sulayman from Kurayb, the mawla of Ibn Abbas, that Abdullah ibn Abbas told him that he had spent a night at the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, who was also Ibn Abbas' mother's sister. Ibn Abbas said, ""I lay down with my head on the breadth of the cushion, and the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and his wife lay down with their heads on its length. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, slept, until, halfway through the night or a little before or after it, he awoke and sat up and wiped the sleep away from his face with his hand. Then he recited the last ten ayats of sura Ali Imran (Sura3). Then he got up and went over to a water-skin which was hanging up and did wudu from it, doing his wudu thoroughly, and then he stood in prayer."" Ibn Abbas continued, ""I stood up and did the same and then went and stood by his side. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, put his right hand on my head and took my right ear and tweaked it. He prayed two rakas, then two rakas, then two rakas, then two rakas, then two rakas, then two rakas, and then prayed an odd raka. Then he lay down until the muadhdhin came to him, and then prayed two quick rakas, and went out and prayed subh"
"265","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from his father that Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhrama told him that Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani said one night that he was going to observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah"
"266","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Abdullah ibn Umar that a man asked the Messenger of Allah"
"267","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Ibn Muhayriz that a man from the Kinana tribe called al-Mukhdaji heard a man in Syria known as Abu Muhammad saying"
"268","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Bakr ibn Umar that Said ibn Yasar said"
"269","Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said"
"270","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that a man asked Abdullah ibn Umar whether the witr was obligatory and Abdullah ibn Umar said"
"271","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that A'isha"
"272","It was narrated to me from Malik, from Nafi', that he said: I was with Abdullah ibn Umar in Mecca, and the sky was cloudy. Abdullah ibn Umar feared that dawn had broken, so he performed Witr with one rak'ah. Then the clouds cleared, and he saw that there was still night remaining. So he prayed two rak'ahs to complete his Witr, and then he prayed two rak'ahs after that. When he feared that dawn had broken, he performed Witr with one rak'ah."
"273","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say the taslim between the two rakas and the one raka of witr so that he could order something he needed"
"274","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas used to pray witr after isha with one raka. Malik said"
"275","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say"
"276","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd al Karim ibn Abi'l-Mukhariq al-Basri from Said ibn Jubayr that Abdullah ibn Abbas slept"
"277","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Ubada ibn as-Samit and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabia had all prayed witr after the break of dawn"
"278","Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that Abdullah ibn Masud said"
"279","Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said"
"280","Yahya related to me from Malik that Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim said"
"281","Malik related to me that Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim heard his father al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say"
"282","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Hafsa"
"283","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said that A'isha"
"284","Yahya related to me from Malik from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman said"
"285","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Umar missed the two rakas of dawn"
"286","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad had done the same as Ibn Umar"
